ose/start operations were bounded functional verification; cmd-56d4dc8e54294c06 left the mount temporarily stopped after its check exited early, and cmd-57f78f1e143744c8 immediately performed the complete validation and restored the active mount. The transient reboot unit was held under /run and disappeared through reboot. Final observations show no failed services, no new listening exposure, healthy package state, and only normal reboot-generated temporary-directory turnover.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0351da845bec447a","cmd-207c2820ce524489","cmd-a4ddea1a00a748c8","cmd-e9049c89007f4a72","cmd-56d4dc8e54294c06","cmd-57f78f1e143744c8","cmd-9b239ce4503342df","cmd-a229a226b75d42ed","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Node1 has a functioning LUKS2-backed XFS volume at /srv/secure, and a directly observed reboot demonstrated automatic unlock, automatic mounting, data persistence, and clean recovery while preserving the original RHEL release and kernel. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and corroborated by the fixed lifecycle boot identities.","limitations":[]}
